CORE
template-eval.sh
--resolve-dynamic-sites --cvc5
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^Dynamic sites: 2 resolved, 0 unreachable, 0 unresolved \(3 rounds\)$
^\[shell-dynamic-site\.1\] .* "echo installing "\*" >&2", "echo installing "\*" >/dev/null": SUCCESS$
^\[shell-unsupported\.1\] .* the parts of the text of eval for the holes of "echo installing "\*" >&2" are words .*: FAILURE$
^\[shell-dynamic-site\.2\] .* "value=\\""\*"\\"": SUCCESS$
^\[shell-unsupported\.3\] .* the parts of the text of eval for the holes of "value=\\""\*"\\"" are words .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.1\] .*: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
A template with holes for the text of eval: each hole is a quoted
reference to a ghost variable that holds its part of the text. The part
is checked to be a word without special characters for its position: an
argument may have blanks (line 8); after that check, the part in double
quotes at line 9 holds, and the assignment is the one of the text.
